        "title": "Simplify PR synchronization to normal Git lease semantics",
        "body": "Simplify `sync_pr` around normal Git lease semantics.\n\nConceptually:\n\n```text\nknown remote head\n  \u2193\ngit push --force-with-lease=<exact-known-head>\n  \u2193\nsuccess or Git rejection\n```\n\nRetain only the metadata needed to identify the correct repository, branch, and expected head.\n\nRemove duplicate remote-head checks, speculative post-push verification, and special retry reconciliation unless a concrete observed failure demonstrates that they are necessary.\n\nExternal branch changes must still never be overwritten: the exact lease remains the authoritative guard.\n\nThis change implements the behavior above with focused regression coverage and documentation.\n\nValidation: deterministic regression tests and independent GitWeave review; GitHub CI on the published changes.\n\nCloses #38."
      }
    },
